s an=20
> attached drive not to be detected as that machine doesn=E2=80=99t suppo=
rt AHCI.
>=20
> Here is the output with the machine Standard PC (Q35 + ICH9, 2009),=20
> which does have AHCI support.

[=E2=80=A6]

> Is that a Linux or QEMU issue?

After selecting the options below and rebuilding the Linux kernel, the=20
disk is detected also in QEMU=E2=80=99s Standard PC (i440FX + PIIX, 1996)=
=2E

CONFIG_ATA_SFF=3Dy
CONFIG_ATA_BMDMA=3Dy
CONFIG_PATA_OLDPIIX=3Dy


Sorry for the noise. Kind regards,

Paul

